   $q$Which two motivations pull Tomas in different directions during the night?$q$, $q$[{"text":"He wants to impress Adaeze as president, and he wants to quit the science club after tonight.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"He wants to stay warm on his blanket, and he wants to finish the clipboard before the clouds arrive.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-narrow"},{"text":"He wants to count every meteor himself, and he wants to let others do the counting.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"He wants big totals to win the scientist's visit, and he wants to be someone a scientist would trust.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$He wants big totals to win the scientist's visit, and he wants to be someone a scientist would trust.$q$, $q$The second paragraph states both goals: he "wanted the totals to be big" for the visit and wanted "to be the kind of person a scientist would trust." Nothing suggests he wants to quit the club or impress Adaeze.$q$, 'draft', '5181c286-dfeb-56ae-b916-e39709050393')
