   $q$The speaker practiced the solo "not to play it better than she did, / but to prove that I could have." What motive does this reveal?$q$, $q$[{"text":"A wish to replace Imani in the concert by learning the part secretly.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"A plan to help Imani by learning the part well enough to coach her.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"A simple love of practice that has nothing to do with Imani at all.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-narrow"},{"text":"Wounded pride: the speaker wants to know she deserved the solo too.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Wounded pride: the speaker wants to know she deserved the solo too.$q$, $q$Practicing "until my fingertips burned" just to prove "I could have" shows hurt pride after the polite, weather-like clapping. Nothing suggests a plan to take over the concert or to coach Imani.$q$, 'draft', '9519b9c5-6bf6-5851-a29a-86e757ab16fe')
