   $q$How does Imani's request in the fourth stanza complicate the speaker's view of their relationship?$q$, $q$[{"text":"It shows that Imani has always looked down on the speaker's playing.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"It shows that Imani is planning to give up the first chair next season.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"It shows that Imani wants to borrow the speaker's cello permanently.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"literal-reading"},{"text":"It reveals that Imani has been copying the speaker too, so the admiration was mutual.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$It reveals that Imani has been copying the speaker too, so the admiration was mutual.$q$, $q$Imani says she "has been trying to copy me for two years," which mirrors the speaker copying her bow arm. The speaker had seen only a one-way rivalry, so this reveal changes things.$q$, 'draft', '9519b9c5-6bf6-5851-a29a-86e757ab16fe')
