   $q$How does the final scene, where the judges first ask who Teodoro is, help develop the story's theme?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Her honest credit becomes the start of the conversation, suggesting that admitting collaboration is a strength, not a weakness.","is_correct":true},{"text":"It suggests that judges care more about a student's age than about the quality of the work itself.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"It suggests that Priya regrets the credit line and wishes she had followed her teacher's advice.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-character-change"},{"text":"It suggests that Priya will lose because she drew attention away from her own work at the showcase.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Her honest credit becomes the start of the conversation, suggesting that admitting collaboration is a strength, not a weakness.$q$, $q$The credit line draws the judges in, and Priya "smiled and told them," showing confidence rather than regret. The story never states the result, so claiming she will lose is unsupported.$q$, 'draft', '94d714ad-1d2b-5673-adb0-305456ae689a')
