insert into public.passages (id, code, skill_id, sat_alignment, grade_band, title, body, status)
values ('6a053eac-0bc2-5347-a207-b0e9e427a623', 'rg10-character-setting-plot-p07', (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g10-character-setting-plot'), null,
        '9-12', $q$My Uncle Draws the River$q$, $q$My uncle Ravi makes maps by hand
in a shop that smells of graphite and old glue.
He measures twice and inks once.
He says a map that lies is worse than no map at all,
and he means it, mostly.

Last spring the city took down the wooden footbridge
and built a new one, wide and white, fifty feet downstream.
Every customer since has asked him to fix it.
Every week he says he will.
Every map still shows the old bridge, exactly where it was.

I asked him once, too directly, why.
He kept his eyes on the paper and told me
that as a boy he sold newspapers on that bridge,
that he learned the whole town by watching it cross.
Then he said the new bridge was fine. He said it twice.

On Saturday I took a fresh sheet and drew the river myself.
I inked the new bridge in black, where it really stands.
Upstream I sketched the old one in light pencil,
thin as breath, the way you draw something
you are not ready to erase.

He studied it for a long time.
Then he picked up his finest pen
and, very carefully, did not touch the pencil.
He only signed his name beneath mine.$q$, 'draft')
