   $q$What conflict does Uncle Ravi face in the poem?$q$, $q$[{"text":"He believes maps must be accurate, but he cannot bring himself to remove the old bridge.","is_correct":true},{"text":"He wants to draw the new bridge, but the city will not tell him where it stands.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"He wants to sell more maps, but customers prefer maps printed by machines.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"He wants to retire from mapmaking, but the speaker wants him to keep the shop.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$He believes maps must be accurate, but he cannot bring himself to remove the old bridge.$q$, $q$He says "a map that lies is worse than no map at all," yet "every map still shows the old bridge." The new bridge's location is known, "fifty feet downstream," so that is not the problem.$q$, 'draft', '6a053eac-0bc2-5347-a207-b0e9e427a623')
